What is Pigment Black?
Pigment Black refers to a class of finely ground carbon-based pigments primarily used to impart deep black coloration across various industries. These pigments are categorized into types such as lamp black, acetylene black, gas black, and others, each offering unique properties like UV resistance, opacity, and chemical stability. Their particle size typically ranges between 20-300 nanometers, enabling superior dispersion in various mediums.

Pigment Black is extensively utilized in applications requiring color consistency and durability, with significant usage in plastics (28% market share), printing inks (24%), and paints (35%). Recent innovations include the development of eco-friendly variants to comply with REACH regulations, with Asia-Pacific dominating production (58% market share in 2024) due to established manufacturing hubs in China and India.

